	(text "Notes:\n- Common ground required: ESP GND = TB6612FNG GND = motor supply GND.\n- Do not power the motor from the ESP 3.3V rail; use a separate, current-limited supply.\n- Do not feed 5V into ESP 3V3 -- it is a regulated OUTPUT, not an input. Power via USB-C or 5Vin.\n- Pin numbers (L1..L22, R1..R22 / L1..L8, R1..R8) are physical header positions matching the real board's left/right headers -- L pins exit the LEFT of each symbol, R pins the RIGHT; see docs/reference/ for the source pinouts.\n- Layout: TB6612FNG (driver) is placed left of the ESP32-S3 (controller) so their facing headers (TB6612 real-right <-> ESP real-left) wire directly across with minimal crossings; motor + PSU sit further left of the driver.\n- Full context: WIRING.md and MILESTONE.md in this experiment's directory."
		(at 98 285 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)))
		(uuid "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000001075")
